"sjdevnull@yahoo.com" <sjdevnull@yahoo.com> wrote:
>1. Make sure you have magic cancellation at level 3, that stops 98% of
>touch stoning

This statement is widely believed, but turns out not to be the case.
The rules for a cockatrice's stoning touch attack are as follows:

If you are hit by a melee attack of damage type AD_STON, you have a one
in three chance of hearing the attacker make a sound. If the attacker
has been cancelled, this sound will be a cough, and no ill effects will
ensue. If the attacker has not been cancelled, the sound will be
hissing.

If you hear a creature hiss when its AD_STON melee attack hits you, and
your current form is not immune to petrification, and you are not
currently already in the process of turning to stone, then you will start
to turn the stone 10% of the time normally, or 100% of the time if you do
not have a lizard corpse in your main inventory *AND* it is a new moon
according to the game's calculations. Again, there is no checking of the
player's magic cancellation score.

The relevant passage in the Nethack 3.4.3 source code is src/mhitu.c lines
1180-1214. Note that the code checks "mtmp->mcan" (whether the monster
has been cancelled) rather than "uncancelled" - the cached result of the
check for the monster having been cancelled or the player's magic
cancellation check having been passed.

Eva Myers' "Myths and Facts about Nethack" page at
  http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/
links to David Corbett's cockatrice spoiler at
  http://www.geocities.com/dcorbett42/nethack/cockatrice.htm
which details the true state of affairs regarding how petrification
attacks work.
